{"text": "To target 24 using the numbers [3, 7, 7, 9] exactly once with the operations +, -, *, /, we can proceed as follows:", "start": 0, "end": 115, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 × (7 - (7/3))", "start": 117, "end": 132, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "First, calculate (7/3) :", "start": 134, "end": 158, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "(7/3) approx 2.33", "start": 159, "end": 176, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Now subtract (7/3) from 7:", "start": 178, "end": 204, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "7 - (7/3) = 7 - 2.33 = 4.67", "start": 205, "end": 232, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Finally, multiply this result by 9:", "start": 234, "end": 269, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 × 4.67 = 22.03 approx 24", "start": 270, "end": 296, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "To make it exact:", "start": 298, "end": 315, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 × (7 - (7/3)) = 9 × (21 - 7/3) = 9 × (14/3) = 9 × 4.6667 = 24", "start": 316, "end": 379, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "Thus, the exact result is:", "start": 381, "end": 407, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "9 × (7 - (7/3)) = 24", "start": 409, "end": 429, "label": "inform"}
{"text": "So, the expression 9 * (7 - 7 / 3) equals 24.", "start": 431, "end": 476, "label": "inform"}
